Priority: 2
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: fix-select-tool

Goal:
Allow the canvas to hold multiple selected objects at once instead of only one active selection target.

Context:
The current selection system is single-target only. The user now wants multi-object editing, which also unlocks batch styling and desktop-style selection behavior.

Expected changes:

- selection-state model for multiple selected targets
- selection overlay behavior for grouped/batch selection
- move interactions that work on the whole selected set

Acceptance criteria:

- More than one supported selectable item can be selected at the same time.
- Moving a multi-selection moves the whole selected set predictably.
- Selection state survives normal redraw and save/load flows without corrupting item identity.

Notes:

- Keep this task focused on selection state and movement; styling and marquee behavior are separate follow-up tasks.
